// D1 round 5 / H8 — A MATCH SCRUTINEE THAT IS A TEMPORARY HELD NOTHING.
//
// This fixture exists because of a MEASUREMENT GAP, not a hunch. H5b (the
// CHECKER-side half of each_pat_binding) had no discriminating test: in every
// shape tried, the SOURCE PLACE's own loan refused independently, so reverting
// H5b alone produced zero reds — mutual redundancy, invisible to one-at-a-time
// controls. The discriminator has to be a destructuring over a TEMPORARY, so
// that no named source binding exists and the PATTERN BINDING is the sole
// holder. Building it found that such a program was ADMITTED:
//
//   let w: Wrap = c.mk_wrap(); match w { Wrap { b: got } => …   rc=1  REFUSED
//   match c.mk_wrap() { Wrap { b: got } => …                    rc=0  ADMITTED
//
// The only difference is whether the scrutinee was NAMED. A named scrutinee
// hands its bindings the loans it already holds (propagate_pat_loans over
// bc_hop_roots); a temporary holds nothing yet, and the loan its own
// evaluation takes (`&self` elision on mk_wrap) was never taken at all,
// because take_ref_borrows — the only site that turns an elided `&self`
// result into a loan — is never called on a scrutinee.
//
// Closed by retain_temp_scrut_loan (borrow_check.cpp), at all THREE spellings
// of the extraction: match statement, match expression, let-else. The loan is
// taken once per construct, held by a synthetic name, and inherited by the
// bindings through the ordinary loan channel.
//
// PAIRED WITH, and all three are required:
//   fail/bc_d1r5_h8_match_named_twin   — the named spelling: INERT, must refuse
//   fail/bc_d1r5_h8_matchexpr_tmp      — the match-as-VALUE spelling
//   pass/bc_d1r5_h8_match_tmp_admits   — read through, THEN mutate (NLL)
//   pass/bc_d1r5_h8_match_scalar_admits— a temporary carrying no loan ties none
//
// ⚠ H5b's UNIQUENESS PROOF LIVES IN THIS GROUP. With each_pat_binding reverted
// to its two-of-thirteen shape (Wild + VariantData only) all three H8 fixtures
// are ADMITTED again — the Struct arm binds nothing, so the retained loan finds
// no holder and dies. They are the first fixtures in the corpus that red under
// the H5b revert at all; the single-rule discriminator is the NAMED twin, which
// reds under the H5b revert and stays green under the H8 revert. Full matrix in
// that fixture's header and at retain_temp_scrut_loan in borrow_check.cpp.
package bc_d1r5_h8_match_tmp_scrutinee;
#[borrow_carrying]
struct B { p: &i64 }
struct C { v: i64 }
struct Wrap { b: B }
impl C {
    fn mk_wrap(&self) -> Wrap { return Wrap { b: B { p: &self.v } }; }
    fn bump(&mut self) { self.v = self.v + 1i64; }
}
fn main() -> i64 {
    let z: i64 = 7i64;
    let mut c: C = C { v: 1i64 };
    let mut inner: B = B { p: &z };
    match c.mk_wrap() { Wrap { b: got } => { inner = got; } }
    c.bump();
    return *inner.p;
}
